WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 11.9 · Fundraising, Revenue & Sustainable Business Models
Major donors

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Build a few personal relationships, staged and planned, or decide major gifts do not fit.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.600
1. Start with people who already give or volunteer.

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.200
2. Plan each prospect’s next step and who leads it.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.200
3. Set boundaries so donors cannot steer your mission.

6
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.800
An example: Riverside Repair Hub (Hybrid · charity with a trading company, United Kingdom)

7
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:31.000
“Riverside: J.R., a volunteer who has given twice, is asked for £3,000 a year to train electrical safety testers.”

8
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.400
You write a staged plan for a few prospects, with boundaries.

9
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.400
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

10
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.000
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
